<concept id="Email_C1_WhatIsAGmailAlertMessage_SD">
  <title>What is a Gmail Alert Message?</title>

  <shortdesc>Learn what Gmail warning banners mean, including why they may
  appear on suspicious emails and how you should respond to potential phishing
  threats.</shortdesc>

  <prolog>
    <author>Sara Davila</author>

    <source
    href="https://oit.ncsu.edu/2022/09/15/gmail-alert-be-careful-with-this-message/">https://oit.ncsu.edu/2022/09/15/gmail-alert-be-careful-with-this-message/</source>
  </prolog>

  <conbody>
    <p>When Gmail identifies an email as potentially suspicious, it may
    display a warning banner that states "Be careful with this message." These
    banners help NC State users recognize messages that may contain malicious
    content or phishing threats. Gmail uses automated security indicators that
    identify messages which are potentially dangerous to users and alerts
    recipients.</p>

    <p>For additional guidance on recognizing suspicious messages, see <xref
    href="Email_T1_HowToAvoidSuspiciousEmails_SD.dita">How to Avoid Suspicious
    Emails</xref>.</p>

    <fig>
      <title>Example of a Gmail Warning Banner</title>

      <image href="images/Gmail-Warning-Flag.png">
        <alt>Yellow Gmail warning banner that displays a warning "Be careful
        with this message" above a suspicious email.</alt>
      </image>
    </fig>

    <section><title>Understanding Gmail Warning Banners</title><p>Gmail might
    display warning banners on messages from unfamiliar senders, or when there
    is a potential threat of phishing. A warning doesn't necessarily mean that
    the email is malicious, but it indicates that the recipient should verify
    the sender and assess the message carefully before interacting with
    it.</p></section>

    <section><title>How to Respond to a Warning Banner</title><p><ul>
        <li>If you have verified that the sender and message are legitimate,
        you can dismiss the warning or you can select the "Looks safe" option
        on the warning banner.</li>

        <li>If you are not familiar with the sender, make sure to examine the
        message carefully before replying, opening any attachments, or
        clicking on any links.</li>

        <li>If you suspect the email is malicious or a phishing attempt, do
        not interact with the content, any links, or any attachments. Report
        the email as phishing by selecting the "Report phishing" button or
        following NC State's <xref
        href="Phishing_T_ReportingPhishing_JB.dita">phishing reporting
        process</xref>.</li>
      </ul><note type="important"><p>Keep in mind that the absence of a
    warning banner in Gmail does not guarantee that an email is safe.
    Suspicious and malicious emails may bypass automated detection. The
    availability and appearance of the warning banner may also look different
    across devices or other email applications.</p></note></p></section>
  </conbody>
</concept>
